# Task: business overview

The owner wants to keep an eye on things: a quick, complete picture of the business, not
details. Use one query, then summarise.

## Steps

1. Run this query with `{{ tools.query }}`:

```graphql
query Overview {
  business { name tagline }
  activeVersion { modified basedOn { number tag createdAt } }
  openReviews: reviews { id note target { collection id field } }
  trash { ref { collection id } label deletedAt }
{% for c in collections if c.list_query != "reviews" %}
  {{ c.list_query }} { id {{ "hidden " if c.hideable else "" }}updatedAt }
{% endfor %}
}
```

2. Present:
   - a **summary table**: one row per kind of record, with how many there are, how many
     are hidden, and (if any) how many are in the trash;
   - **Open questions**: the open review items as a table (id, what it is about, note),
     most important first;
   - **Recently changed**: the five most recently updated records across all kinds
     (kind, id, when);
   - **Version status**: which snapshot the active version is based on, and whether
     there are unsaved changes (`modified`).
3. Point out anything that needs attention (open questions, unsaved changes, items in
   the trash), without going into detail.

